## Purpose

This runbook documents the frozen baseline configuration of the **Home Internet Outage Monitoring** Grafana dashboard. The dashboard provides three complementary views:

- whether the gateway and external targets were reachable at a given time;
- whether latency degraded before or during an incident; and
- the rolling availability of an external target over the preceding hour.

Use the dashboard to help distinguish a local gateway/LAN problem, a WAN/ISP outage, an isolated destination failure, severe latency, and a monitoring-data gap. It is an observational aid; correlate its results with router, firewall, ISP, and monitoring-stack evidence before assigning root cause.

## Architecture and data flow

```text
ICMP/HTTP probe targets
  ├─ 192.168.1.1  (local gateway)
  ├─ 1.1.1.1      (external target)
  ├─ 8.8.8.8      (external target)
  └─ google.com    (latency query only, when present in Prometheus)
          │
          ▼
Blackbox Exporter
  Generates probe_success and probe_duration_seconds
          │
          ▼
Prometheus
  Scrapes the Blackbox Exporter under job="internet" and stores time series
          │
          ▼
Grafana 12.4
  Queries Prometheus and renders state, latency, and rolling availability
```

The key metric semantics are:

| Metric | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `probe_success` | `1` when the probe succeeded; `0` when it failed |
| `probe_duration_seconds` | Total probe duration in seconds |

